# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the provider you have.
# `.env` is gitignored, so never commit real API keys.
#
# You do not have to write this by hand. `viral-bench init` asks which provider
# you want, writes the key into `.env` for you, and records the model each stage
# uses in config/local.yaml. `viral-bench doctor` then checks everything a real
# run needs before you spend anything. There is deliberately no default provider,
# because ViralBench ships no model and presumes no account.
#
# Keys are read from the process environment first, then from this file, so an
# `export` always wins over what is written here. The full provider list lives
# in src/viral_bench/providers/spec.py, and a representative handful is below.

# --- Hosted providers -------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=            # https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=         # https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# GEMINI_API_KEY=            # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=        # https://openrouter.ai/keys
#
# The rest follow the same <PROVIDER>_API_KEY shape: GROQ_API_KEY,
# TOGETHER_API_KEY, FIREWORKS_API_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, XAI_API_KEY,
# MISTRAL_API_KEY. `viral-bench models` lists every provider and marks the ones
# you already hold a credential for.

# Optional: the crowd checks GEMINI_API_KEY_CROWD before GEMINI_API_KEY, so its
# (potentially large) token spend can be budgeted on a key of its own.
# GEMINI_API_KEY_CROWD=

# --- Local models -----------------------------------------------------------
# Ollama needs no key: it is usable as soon as `ollama serve` is running. Set
# this only if it is not on the default port.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# --- Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint -----------------------------------
# A gateway, a proxy, vLLM, a server a colleague runs: all of these are the
# `custom` provider, which has no built-in URL and so needs both variables.
# CUSTOM_BASE_URL=https://your-endpoint.example.com/v1
# CUSTOM_API_KEY=

# --- Redirecting a provider's endpoint --------------------------------------
# Every provider's base URL can be overridden with <PROVIDER>_BASE_URL, which is
# the provider id upper-cased, hyphens turned into underscores. This is the escape
# hatch for a proxy, a gateway or a regional endpoint: it changes where the call
# goes, not which key authenticates it.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://my-gateway.example.com/v1
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=

# --- Providers that use ambient credentials ---------------------------------
# `google-vertex` and `google-vertex-anthropic` take no API key. They use cloud
# application-default credentials. Run `gcloud auth application-default login`
# rather than putting anything here. Optional overrides:
# VERTEX_PROJECT=
# VERTEX_LOCATION=global
